From 1ed0c7cf8028cac2188c875818bac34882b43eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:45:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TileLang split-K in one launch, blocked accumulation,
 per-bucket tiles

- bf16_gemm_splitk: every CTA writes its shard's partial, and the last CTA of
  each tile (an acq_rel arrival count after a device-scope fence) adds the
  shards in order into the outputs: splitk_reduce's bits without its launch.
  TileLangSplitLinearMethod uses it for decode rows; per-layer counters stay
  zeroed between calls.
- blocked accumulation (opt-in on the BF16 kernels): each K block is summed on
  its own and then added, which shortens the FP32 chains. SPLIT_BF16 now
  selects shards and blocking per shape (five shards, blocked).
- SPLIT_FP8 decode tiles by row bucket, with window 2's sweep winners, and the
  context KV's prefill tile.
- A layer may serve more than DECODE_ROWS rows on decode tiles (padded to whole
  64-row tiles); the WO projection's weights serve up to 128.
Every other projection compiles to the same code as before.
